          "driveFiles": [
            {
              "id": "1DzNiP_tzQbbIZrsm7c42-TaW0LZXTaDC",
              "name": "Renal-Acute kidney injury.pdf",
              "folder": "Chapter 5 Renal",
              "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DzNiP_tzQbbIZrsm7c42-TaW0LZXTaDC/view",
              "totalPages": 18,
              "rawText": "FILE: Renal-Acute kidney injury.pdf\nFOLDER: Chapter 5 Renal\nDRIVE_URL: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DzNiP_tzQbbIZrsm7c42-TaW0LZXTaDC/view\nTOTAL_PAGES: 18\n\n--- [Page 1] ---\nACUTE KIDNEY INJURY\nPONGSIRI KULCHANAWICHIEN, PHARM.D.\nPHARMA PLUS INSTITUTE\n\n--- [Page 2] ---\nDEFINITION\n A sudden, sustained, and usually reversible decrease \nin the glomerular filtration rate (GFR) occurring over a \nperiod of hours to days.\n KDIGO Definition of AKI ( 2012) \n Increase in SCr by ≥ 0.3 mg/dL within 48 hours\n Increase in Scr by ≥ 1.5 times baseline, which is known or \npresumed to have occurred within the prior seven days\n Urine volume <0.5 mL/kg/h for six hours\nPONGSIRI KULCHANAWICHIEN, PHARM.D.\n2\nScr, BUN ↑ แต่ eGFR ↓\n\n--- [Page 3] ---\nDEFINITION\n Azotemia is an elevation of blood urea nitrogen \n(BUN) and serum creatinine levels\n Oliguria is defined as a urine output that is less than \n400 mL daily in adults\n Anuria is defined as a urine output that is less than \n100 mL daily in adults\nPONGSIRI KULCHANAWICHIEN, PHARM.D.\n3\n\n--- [Page 4] ---\nSTAGE OF AKI\nPONGSIRI KULCHANAWICHIEN, PHARM.D.\n4\nKDIGO guideline 2012\n\n--- [Page 5] ---\nCONCEPTUAL MODEL FOR AKI\nPONGSIRI KULCHANAWICHIEN, PHARM.D.\n5\nKDIGO guideline 2012\n\n--- [Page 6] ---\nGENERAL TREATMENT\n Identify and correct cause of AKI\n Correct fluid balance\n Closely monitor Scr and urine output \n Avoid nephrotoxic agents\n Consider renal replacement therapy\nPONGSIRI KULCHANAWICHIEN, PHARM.D.\n6\n\n--- [Page 7] ---\nCAUSES OF AKI\nPONGSIRI KULCHANAWICHIEN, PHARM.D.\n7\nKDIGO guideline 2012\n\n--- [Page 8] ---\nCAUSES OF AKI\nPONGSIRI KULCHANAWICHIEN, PHARM.D.\n8\n\n--- [Page 9] ---\nPHASE OF ATN\nPONGSIRI KULCHANAWICHIEN, PHARM.D.\n9\n\n--- [Page 10] ---\nLABORATORY TESTING\nPre-Renal AKI Intrinsic AKI\nBUN/Scr > 20 < 10\nUrine Sp gr > 1.020 < 1.010\nUrine Osm > 500 250-300\nUrine Na < 20 > 40\nFE Na < 1% > 1%\nUrine sediment Inactive Active\n➢ Tubular epithelial cells\n➢ Granular casts\nPONGSIRI KULCHANAWICHIEN, PHARM.D.\n10\nFE Na (Fractional Excretion of Sodium)\n\n--- [Page 11] ---\nGOAL\n Maintain fluid and electrolyte\n Provide nutritional support\n Prevent or treat complications\nPONGSIRI KULCHANAWICHIEN, PHARM.D.\n11\n\n--- [Page 12] ---\nMANAGEMENT\n Identify and correct causes\n Optimize cardiac output and renal blood flow\n Avoid nephrotoxic drug: adjust doses and monitor \nconcentrations where appropriate\n Monitor fluid balance, renal function and body weight\nPONGSIRI KULCHANAWICHIEN, PHARM.D.\n12\n\n--- [Page 13] ---\nMANAGEMENT\n Treat complication\n Hyperkalemia\n Avoids drug induce hyperkalemia\n Avoids high potassium diet\n Hypocalcemia > Calcium supplement\n Pulmonary edema\n Metabolic acidosis > Sodium bicarbonate if pH < 7.1\nPONGSIRI KULCHANAWICHIEN, PHARM.D.\n13\n\n--- [Page 14] ---\nMANAGEMENT\n Nutrition support: adequate calories, minimal nitrogenous \nwaste production, potassium restriction\n Energy: 25-30 Kcal/kg/day\n Protein intake\n 0.8–1.0 g/kg/d of protein in noncatabolic AKI patients without \nneed for dialysis\n 1.0–1.5 g/kg/d in patients with AKI on RRT\n Up to a maximum of 1.7 g/kg/d in patients on continuous \nrenal replacement therapy (CRRT) and in hypercatabolic \npatients.\n Diuretic (avoid in dehydrate patient)\n Loop diuretic\nPONGSIRI KULCHANAWICHIEN, PHARM.D.\n14\n\n--- [Page 15] ---\nMANAGEMENT\n Identify and aggressively treat infection\n Identify and treat bleeding tendency\n Initiate dialysis\nPONGSIRI KULCHANAWICHIEN, PHARM.D.\n15\n\n--- [Page 16] ---\nMANAGEMENT\nPONGSIRI KULCHANAWICHIEN, PHARM.D.\n16\n\n--- [Page 17] ---\nMANAGEMENT\n Suggest using isotonic crystalloids rather than \ncolloids (albumin or starches) as initial management \nfor expansion of intravascular volume\n Control blood sugar 110-149 mg/dl \n Not recommend NAC to prevent AKI in critically ill \npatients with hypotension\n Assess at 3 months after AKI for resolution or \nworsening to CKD\nPONGSIRI KULCHANAWICHIEN, PHARM.D.\n17"
            }
          ],
          "quickSummaryHtml": "<div style=\"line-height: 1.75;\">\n  <div class=\"tip\" style=\"margin-top:0;\">\n    <b>สรุปด่วนหัวใจสำคัญ Acute Kidney Injury (Slides P.1–18 + บรรยาย อ.พงศิริ + KDIGO / Trials 2018–2026):</b>\n    <ul style=\"margin-bottom:0;\">\n      <li><strong>นิยาม KDIGO 2012 &amp; Staging [P.2–5]:</strong> เข้า 1/3 ข้อ = <code>SCr &ge; 0.3</code> (48h) | <code>&ge; 1.5x</code> (7d) | <code>UOP &lt; 0.5 mL/kg/h x 6h</code> (<b>SCr/BUN &uarr;, eGFR &darr;</b>; Oliguria &lt;400, Anuria &lt;100 mL/d); <b>Stage 3:</b> SCr <mark><b>&ge;3x หรือ &ge;4.0 หรือ RRT</b></mark>; Biomarkers ขึ้นก่อน SCr: <b>NGAL, KIM-1, IL-18</b>; AKI ย้อนกลับได้ (<b>Reversible</b>)</li>\n      <li><strong>กลไกยา &amp; สาเหตุ 3 กลุ่ม [P.7–8]:</strong> <b>Prerenal:</b> NSAIDs/CNI <b>หด Afferent</b> | ACEI/ARB <b>ขยาย Efferent</b> | ห้าม <b>Triple Whammy (Diuretic+ACEI/ARB+NSAID)</b> | <b>Intrinsic ATN (85%):</b> Ischemia, Sepsis, <b>Aminoglycosides, AmB, Contrast, Cisplatin, Vanc</b>; <b>AIN Triad:</b> ไข้-ผื่น-Eosinophiluria | <b>Postrenal &amp; Crystal:</b> Acyclovir/MTX/Sulfa</li>\n      <li><strong>แล็บแยก Prerenal vs ATN &amp; 4 ระยะ [P.9–10]:</strong> Prerenal (<b>BUN:SCr &gt;20, Sp.Gr &gt;1.020, U.Osm &gt;500, U.Na &lt;20, FENa &lt;1%</b>) vs ATN (<b>&lt;10, &lt;1.010, 250–300, &gt;40, &gt;1%, Muddy brown casts &amp; RTE cells</b>); ได้ยาขับปัสสาวะใช้ <b>FEUrea (&lt;35% vs &gt;50%)</b>; ระยะ <b>Recovery (Diuretic phase)</b> ระวังขาดน้ำ/K<sup>+</sup>/Mg<sup>2+</sup></li>\n      <li><strong>รักษาประคับประคอง &amp; ฟอกไต AEIOU [P.11–17]:</strong> เริ่ม <b>Isotonic crystalloids</b> (<b>Balanced LR/Acetar</b> &gt; NSS ปริมาณมาก), งด Colloids/HES; <mark><b>ห้าม Loop diuretic ป้องกัน AKI หรือในคน Dehydration!</b></mark>; DTX <b>110–149</b>; งด NAC (PRESERVE); นัดซ้ำ <b>3 เดือน</b>; <b>AEIOU:</b> Acidosis (pH &lt;7.1–7.2), Electrolytes (HyperK/<b>HyperMg</b>), Intoxication (<b>SLIME + Theophylline/Phenobarbital</b>), Overload, Uremia; <b>STARRT-AKI:</b> ไม่รีบฟอกถ้าไม่มี AEIOU</li>\n      <li><strong>Hyperkalemia 3-Step &amp; ป้องกันพิษจากยา [P.8, 12–13]:</strong> K<sup>+</sup> วิกฤต &rarr; (1) <b>IV 10% Ca gluconate</b> (ไม่ลด K<sup>+</sup>), (2) <b>RI+D50W / Salbutamol</b>, (3) <b>Kayexalate/SZC/Dialysis</b> | <b>AmB:</b> ต้อง <b>0.9% NSS Pre/Post 500–1,000 mL</b> | <b>CIN:</b> 0.9% NSS ดีสุด (<b>Metformin:</b> ACR ใหม่ <b>eGFR &lt;30/AKI/IA หยุด 48h</b> vs ข้อสอบเดิมหยุดทุกคน 48h) | <b>Vanc:</b> AUC/MIC 400–600 (<b>ACORN:</b> +PTZ ไม่เพิ่ม AKI)</li>\n    </ul>\n  </div>\n</div>",
